**Responsibilities:**
--------------------- Working with the development team, you will be responsible for the design, development, documentation, testing and delivery of the software solution for an Automatic Fare Collection (AFC) system or a high volume and performance intensive back office of an AFC system.

The activities required to be performed shall include the following:

* Requirements gathering;
* Design, development, and maintenance of the software;
* Preparation and submission of deliverables throughout the software development lifecycles such as Business Rules, Software Requirement Specifications, Software Architecture Document, Design Specification, Interface Specifications, Source Codes, Testing Specification, Operation and Maintenance Manual, Training Manual and others documents as required in the standard adopted by the Authority;
* Assist the Authority with day-to-day application support issues; and
* Liaise with users on the requirement, design and testing issues.
**Qualifications \\& Requirements:**
-----------------------------------

* Recognised degree in Computer Science, IT or engineering with at least 5 years’ relevant experience in software development;
* Gone through at least one full software development lifecycle (SDLC) with experience in producing SDLC documentations;
* Extensive experience in analysing requirements, designing, development and delivering complex enterprise applications in Java/JEE, web programming on UNIX / LINUX and Windows environment;
* Proficiency with database programming such as SQL and DAO, and relevant experience with MySQL, PostgreSQL
* Experience in Spring Framework and Spring Boot;
* Experience in Software Modernization, Containerization, Microservices;
* Experience in Agile development methodology and continuous integration;
* Experience in writing Requirements Specification, Use Cases, Design Documentation, object-oriented software design and UML modelling;
* Proficiency in AWS ECS and Docker containerization, with a solid understanding of DevOps principles and best practices
* Added advantage if candidate is familiar with one or more of the following technologies:

i.Experience in Message Queues and/or Solace; ii.Experience in Cloud Computing, Kubernetes \\& Dockers, AWS Services like Amazon ECS Fargate, AWS RDS \\& Lambda; iii. Experience in Automatic Fare Collection (AFC) system; iv.Experience in EMV and Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS); v.Experience in Microsoft Active Directory vi.Experience in HTML / CSS / JavaScript / JSON vii.Experience in Secure Communications (SFTP, HTTPS, etc.) viii.Experience in Angular or equivalent ix.Experience in Java Unit Tests frameworks

**About Us** APTIH has been established since year 2012. Our headquarter is aptly located in one of the busiest global financial hub, with the ease of outreach to innovation and new technologies. We do envision the firm to play an active role to assist startups to accelerate and to bring their unique value proposition to the global stage. Since our inception, we have been actively involved in investing as well as mentoring new companies in their route to success.

At APTIH, we welcome passionate and proactive startups who are venturing into the Medical, Education and Environment space. We resonate with the global’s emphasis in medical, education and environment to ensure relevance in the ever changing digital landscape.

Centre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies.

For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are seeking a Research Assistant / Research Associate to contribute towards the daily operational needs and strategic research priorities of the NTU Centre of AI in Medicine (C-AIM). The role will support the smooth running of C-AIM’s infrastructure, AVIT systems, administrative processes, procurement, audits, documentation, and coordination activities, ensuring that the Centre’s day-to-day functions are reliable, efficient, and responsive to project and stakeholder needs.

In parallel, the candidate will provide data science and AI/ML modelling support for strategic healthcare AI projects, including clinical and biomedical data preparation, feature engineering, statistical modelling, machine learning model development, validation, performance evaluation, workflow prototyping, reproducible analysis, technical documentation, grant and proposal support, and coordination with internal and external collaborators. Through this dual operational and research-facing role, the candidate will help C-AIM translate AI innovations into practical healthcare applications that advance patient care, health system improvement, and responsible AI implementation in medicine.

**Primary Responsibilities**
 Daily Operations, Infrastructure and AVIT Support

* Manage, operate and maintain C-AIM’s AVIT, computing and infrastructure resources, including microaccess laboratories and AI simulation rooms, to ensure readiness for meetings, events, demonstrations, teaching, research activities and stakeholder engagements;
* Provide day-to-day technical support, troubleshooting and liaison with institutional teams, vendors and service providers for equipment setup, servicing, procurement and upgrades;
* Maintain inventories, usage records, documentation and operational trackers to support efficient centre operations, audit readiness and continuity of services.

Data Science, AI/ML Modelling and Technical Research Support

* Support healthcare AI projects involving statistical modelling, machine learning, predictive analytics, natural language processing, multimodal data integration or other AI/ML approaches relevant to clinical, biomedical or health system applications;
* Assist with data extraction, cleaning, harmonisation, feature engineering, exploratory analysis, model training, validation, benchmarking, calibration and performance evaluation using appropriate statistical and machine learning methods;
* Develop, test and document reproducible analytical workflows, scripts, notebooks, pipelines, dashboards or prototypes to support AI/ML model development and evaluation in healthcare settings;
* Prepare technical summaries, model outputs, visualisations and interpretation notes to support research meetings, grant applications, project reports, manuscripts and stakeholder-facing communications.

Healthcare AI Implementation and Project Support

* Support strategic healthcare AI implementation projects by assisting with needs assessment, workflow mapping, stakeholder documentation, user feedback collection and translation of research findings into practical implementation recommendations;
* Assist with data preparation, processing, statistical analysis, model development, validation, evaluation and documentation for AI-enabled healthcare projects, ensuring that technical outputs are robust, interpretable and aligned with clinical or implementation needs;
* Contribute to the development, testing and evaluation of AI/ML workflows, prototypes, dashboards or tools that support responsible deployment, monitoring or evaluation of AI applications in healthcare settings;
* Support deployment, testing and maintenance of AI/ML applications on suitable institutional or cloud-based platforms, in coordination with relevant technical, governance and stakeholder teams.

Research Coordination, Documentation and Communication

* Prepare and maintain research protocols, study materials, implementation notes, project reports, presentation materials and progress updates for C-AIM projects;
* Coordinate communication across data science teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, technical partners, vendors and administrative units to support timely project delivery and clear stakeholder engagement;
* Support the preparation of grant applications, research proposals, conference materials, posters, manuscripts, ethics submissions and other outputs arising from healthcare AI, data science and AI/ML modelling work.

Research Administration, Compliance and Centre Support

* Handle procurement, purchase requests, vendor coordination, asset tracking and resource planning for both routine centre operations and research project needs;
* Support audits, compliance checks, institutional reporting and documentation processes to ensure alignment with NTU, C-AIM and project governance requirements;
* Assist with research and legal agreements, project records, ethics or governance submissions where applicable, and coordination of administrative workflows required for collaborative healthcare AI projects;
* Coordinate with finance, procurement, human resources, estates, IT and other administrative departments to resolve operational matters and support smooth centre functioning.

**Required Competencies And Qualifications**
* Bachelor’s (for Research Assistant) or Master’s (for Research Associate) degree in Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Health Informatics, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, Applied Mathematics, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or a closely related quantitative discipline relevant to healthcare AI and AI/ML modelling.
* Training or experience in data science, statistical analysis, machine learning, predictive modelling, natural language processing, deep learning, biomedical data analysis, clinical data analytics or related AI/ML methods.
* Ability to support healthcare AI studies involving data preparation, feature engineering, model development, validation, benchmarking, calibration, performance evaluation, interpretability analysis and translation of technical outputs into actionable research insights.
* Competence in preparing, cleaning, organising and analysing structured or unstructured datasets, including clinical, biomedical, imaging, omics, text, survey, workflow, interaction-log or implementation outcome data where applicable.
* Proficiency or strong working familiarity with programming and data analysis tools such as Python, R, SQL, Git, Jupyter notebooks, machine learning libraries, statistical packages, visualisation tools or equivalent platforms is expected.
* Experience with reproducible analytical workflows, model documentation, experiment tracking, version control, data governance, privacy-aware analysis or deployment-oriented AI/ML workflows is advantageous.
* Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical documentation, research protocols, analytical reports, grant or proposal inputs, presentations, ethics documents and stakeholder-facing updates clearly and accurately.
* Good interpersonal and coordination skills, with the ability to liaise professionally with research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, technical partners, vendors and administrative units across multidisciplinary healthcare AI projects.
* Practical ability or willingness to support daily centre operations, including AVIT setup, equipment readiness, infrastructure coordination, inventory tracking, procurement documentation, audit preparation and liaison with vendors or institutional service teams.
* Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and interest in healthcare, AI in medicine, responsible AI implementation, digital health, clinical data science, biomedical AI, machine learning or health system improvement.

